From aa5539adfb02374f3138809ab75c26c8f25a9c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:14:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/32] Plugins: the world around the player (events:world)

A plugin with the permission "events:world" (a map, a pet tracker) hears
a2.on("world") at most four times a second, and every two seconds while
there is anything: the zone, where the player is, the monsters around
with their npc id and place, and the objects around (gathering spots,
Hidden Cubes ...) with their object id and place, in world units (cm).

The game sends the player's own position only with some actions, so the
position is the last exact report (an action pose, an effect the player
puts on, a teleport or loading screen) for 4 s, and after that the middle
of the entities that moved or appeared around him (about 10 m off), not
taken when it lies further from the last report than he could have
walked. The frame layouts and the estimate follow SkeeveAN's
Aion-DPS-Meter (MIT), where they were checked against recordings.

The frame tap now also runs while such a plugin is loaded; the frames are
read in plugins/world.rs, the snapshot goes out from the plugin event
thread. Unit tests with frames built to those layouts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
